<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="page-intro">
  <p class="eyebrow">FROM OUR PANTRY TO YOURS</p>
  <h1>A few good questions.</h1>
  <b><img src="/images/nut-butter-spoon.gif" alt="" width="175" height="175"></b>
  <p>A little help before your next spoonful.</p>
</section>

<section class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>Are your nut butters homemade?</summary>
      <p>Yes! Our nut butters are handcrafted in small batches right here in Mesa, Arizona. Stonebridge Nut Butters operates under the Arizona Cottage Food Program, allowing us to prepare our products in a home kitchen.</p>
      <p>We take pride in creating fresh, delicious nut butters with thoughtfully selected ingredients.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What ingredients do you use?</summary>
      <p>We start every nut butter blend with roasted peanuts and <strong>no added oils</strong>.</p>
      <p>Our flavored varieties feature a delicious combination of nuts, seeds, sweeteners, and other flavorful ingredients to create their unique taste.</p>
      <p>For a complete list of ingredients, please visit each product's individual listing.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Do your products contain allergens?</summary>
      <p>Our peanut butter products contain <strong>peanuts</strong>, a major food allergen.</p>
      <p>Additional allergens may be present depending on the ingredients used in each flavor. Please review the ingredient and allergen information on each product's label before consuming.</p>
      <p>If you have a food allergy or dietary concern, please contact us before purchasing.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How should I store my nut butter?</summary>
      <p>Our nut butters are made fresh and can be stored in a cool, dry place.</p>
      <p>Natural oil separation may occur over time—this is completely normal! Simply give your nut butter a good stir to restore its smooth, creamy consistency.</p>
      <p>Refrigeration can help minimize oil separation but will also result in a firmer texture. For the best freshness and flavor, we recommend enjoying your nut butter within 2 months of production.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why is there oil on top of my nut butter?</summary>
      <p>A little oil separation is perfectly natural! Because we don't add stabilizing oils to our nut butter base, the peanuts' natural oils may rise to the surface over time.</p>
      <p>Simply give your nut butter a good stir to bring back that delicious, creamy consistency. It's all part of the natural nut butter experience!</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Where do you ship?</summary>
      <p>Stonebridge Nut Butters operates under Arizona's Cottage Food Program, so we're currently able to ship only within Arizona.</p>
      <p>We offer a flat shipping rate of <strong>$7.95 per order</strong> anywhere in the state.</p>
      <p>Prefer to skip shipping? <strong>Free local pickup is available in Mesa, Arizona!</strong></p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How does local pickup work?</summary>
      <p>We offer free local pickup in Mesa, Arizona!</p>
      <p>Simply select the pickup option during checkout, and we'll provide instructions for collecting your order once it's ready.</p>
      <p>Please wait for your pickup confirmation before heading our way!</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Do you accept returns or exchanges?</summary>
      <p>Because our nut butters are food products, we're unable to accept returns or exchanges.</p>
      <p>However, your satisfaction matters to us! If your order arrives damaged or something isn't quite right, please contact us so we can help make it right.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Will my basket be saved?</summary>
      <p>Your shopping basket is automatically saved in your browser, so you can come back later and pick up right where you left off!</p>
      <p>Just keep in mind that clearing your browser data may remove your saved basket, and your basket won't transfer between devices.</p>
    </details>
</section>

